Akamai launched Akamai Inference and Akamai Agent Sandbox on Oct 27. Agents run on Akamai Functions, and the code they write runs in a separate WebAssembly-isolated space with limits on compute, memory, outbound connections and system access. The sandbox ships as an open-source part of the Spin framework, and Akamai says controls on what agents can reach are coming next.

Sources:
https://akamai.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/akamai-launches-ai-inference-service-and-agent-execution

