IBM made Agent Identity generally available on Oct 26. It puts AI agents in a central inventory with an owner, a risk class and approved tool connections, keeps on-behalf-of delegation traceable to the person who started the action, and swaps standing access for short-lived, task-scoped OAuth tokens. Same day, Fortinet added inline checks on prompts, MCP tool calls and agent actions to its firewalls: the week everyone decided agents need papers.

